  {
    "text": "Related technical pipelines for motion tracking and teleoperation rely on a predefined human skeleton structure, requiring skeleton-conditional model training.",
    "topic": "motion tracking"
  },
  {
    "text": "These skeleton-dependent methods struggle to generalize to diverse characters, such as animals from different species, while preserving their unique motion styles.",
    "topic": "generalization"
  },
  {
    "text": "Labeled data for diverse skeleton structures is limited, restricting large-scale training for the task.",
    "topic": "data availability"
  },
  {
    "text": "Most existing frameworks for motion tracking and teleoperation are validated on compact platforms or without real payload interaction.",
    "topic": "validation"
  },
  {
    "text": "Full-size humanoid robots with real payloads have largely unexplored applications for scalable humanoid skill acquisition through general motion tracking and teleoperation.",
    "topic": "humanoid robots"
  }
]
